  ('260425035781022655', 'Forbidden Love Game', 1975, 'Comedy, Crime, Drama', 'Eloy de la Iglesia, Antonio Cuevas', 'Antonio Corencia, Juan Antonio Porto, Eloy de la Iglesia', 'Javier Escrivá, Inma de Santis, John Moulder-Brown, Simón Andreu, Joaquín Pamplona, Blaki, Paul Benson, Francisco José Escrivá', null, 'The film begins with a school teacher bidding farewell to his students, who are leaving for the summer. As he is heading home he notices two of his students are hitch-hiking and picks them up. He invites them over for dinner and lodging, which they accept.. The majority of the film from this point on is set at the mansion, where the two students turn from guests to prisoners under the teacher''s command.', 'The film begins with a school teacher bidding farewell to his students, who are leaving for the summer. As he is heading home he notices two of his students are hitch-hiking and picks them up. He invites them over for dinner and lodging, which they accept.. The majority of the film from this point on is set at the mansion, where the two students turn from guests to prisoners under the teacher''s command.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/5rPeEbCqIqStby4IuTVcJJGoJ4O.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:80296'),
  ('27119604301862797', 'Forbidden Love: The Unashamed Stories of Lesbian Lives', 1992, 'Documentary, History', 'Lynne Fernie, Aerlyn Weissman, Zoe Dirse', 'Aerlyn Weissman, Lynne Fernie', 'Stephanie Morgenstern, Lynne Adams, Marie-Jo Thério, George Thomas, Lory Wainberg, Ann-Marie MacDonald, Keely Moll, Stephanie Ozard', null, 'Ten women in Canada talk about being lesbian in the 1940s, 1950s, and 1960s: discovering the pulp fiction of the day about women in love, their own first affairs, the pain of breaking up, frequenting gay bars, facing police raids, men''s responses, and the etiquette of butch and femme roles. Interspersed among the interviews and archival footage are four dramatized chapters from a pulp novel, "Forbidden Love".', 'Ten women in Canada talk about being lesbian in the 1940s, 1950s, and 1960s: discovering the pulp fiction of the day about women in love, their own first affairs, the pain of breaking up, frequenting gay bars, facing police raids, men''s responses, and the etiquette of butch and femme roles. Interspersed among the interviews and archival footage are four dramatized chapters from a pulp novel, "Forbidden Love".', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/aoTA6sJT3NwOmaZVfMB8PKeeQiK.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:194926'),
  ('650042631056182972', 'Forbidden Passion', 1974, 'Romance, Drama', 'Francisco Lara Polop, Raúl Pérez Cubero', 'Manuel Summers, Francisco Lara Polop, Francisco Summers', 'Ornella Muti, Philippe Leroy, Emilio Gutiérrez Caba, Lina Canalejas, José Vivó, Curro Martín Summers, David Lara, Yelena Samarina', null, 'A young woman was seduced by a high positioned official who is married but when she falls in love with a young man she tries to break the other relationship...', 'A young woman was seduced by a high positioned official who is married but when she falls in love with a young man she tries to break the other relationship...', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3h3oirHfg7ENfvRMqckNyALknIX.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:103137'),
